      "content": "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi lived from 1869 to 1948 and played a central role in India's freedom movement.",
        "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945) and Bhagat Singh (1907–1931) represented revolutionary streams of the freedom struggle.",
        "Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858) was a key figure in the early resistance during the 19th century.",
        "The extremist triumvirate Lal-Bal-Pal comprised Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920), and Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932).",
        "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950) and Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964) were central figures in the national movement and post-independence nation-building."
      ],
      "id": "elmzc3i"
    },
